Z||000000||Bruce||04-03-2000||03:03 PM||||On Suday, April 30, Half Moon Bay (CA.) is hosting the annual "Great American Dream Machines" at the HMB airport. I went last year and really enjoyed seeing the vintage autos, planes, and other assorted vehicles. No Fieros were shown, however, so time for Calif. owners to make an appearance. I'ld do it except I'm too protective of mine.<BR>Hope some of you make it. It's right along the coast, off HWY 1.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-03-2000||03:40 PM||||Thanks for posting that Bruce.  It would be nice if the Golden Gate Fiero Culb could caravan down to the show. if not be in it!!!<P>Whata ya say George??   A little funm in the sun?||||reg||10
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-03-2000||10:03 PM||||Hey Dad, if I had my Fiero I would consider going but unfortunatly as I was about to put my GT in the shop one of my customers clutch went out so my last clutch is going to him. I ordered a few more since they are selling very fast and everybody likes them better then previous clutche that they have installed. This customers clutch went out after just driving less than 10,000 miles. No I did not install that one. It waas installed by a dealer.||||reg||1
